...RECON FINDS FAUSTO STILL A HURRICANE WITH 85 MPH WINDS...
 
 
SUMMARY OF 1100 AM HST...2100 UTC...INFORMATION
-----------------------------------------------
LOCATION...19.9N 142.4W
ABOUT 825 MI...1330 KM E OF HILO HAWAII
MAXIMUM SUSTAINED WINDS...85 MPH...140 KM/H
PRESENT MOVEMENT...W OR 280 DEGREES AT 14 MPH...22 KM/H
MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE...984 MB...29.06 INCHES
 
 
WATCHES AND WARNINGS
--------------------
There are no coastal watches or warnings in effect.
 
Interests in the Hawaiian Islands should monitor the progress of
Fausto.
 
 
DISCUSSION AND OUTLOOK
----------------------
At 1100 AM HST (2100 UTC), the center of Hurricane Fausto was
located by Air Force Reserve reconnaissance aircraft near latitude
19.9 North, longitude 142.4 West. Fausto is moving toward the west
near 14 mph (22 km/h), and a general westward to west-northwestward
motion is expected to continue for the next several days.
 
Maximum sustained winds remain near 85 mph (140 km/h) with higher 
gusts. Gradual weakening is forecast during the next several days.
 
Hurricane-force winds extend outward up to 35 miles (55 km) from the
center and tropical-storm-force winds extend outward up to 150 miles
(240 km).
 
The minimum central pressure estimated by aircraft dropsonde data is 
984 mb (29.06 inches).
 
 
HAZARDS AFFECTING LAND
----------------------
Key messages for Fausto can be found in the Tropical Cyclone
Discussion under AWIPS header HFOTCDCP1 and WMO header WTPA41 PHFO.
 
SURF: Surf generated by Fausto is expected to begin building across
east-facing shores of the eastern end of Hawaii today, spreading
westward tonight into Monday, and continue building through Tuesday
as Fausto approaches and moves into the area. These swells are
likely to cause life-threatening surf and rip current conditions.
Please consult products from your local weather office.
 
 
NEXT ADVISORY
-------------
Next complete advisory at 500 PM HST.
 
